import Mathlib

/-!
# A characteristic ideal does not bound the coinvariants

This file records, formally, the counterexample to the Iwasawa-theoretic step that a unit
leading coefficient of a characteristic power series bounds the size of the coinvariant group
produced by a control theorem.

## The situation

For `E/Q` and a prime `p`, the dual `p^∞`-Selmer group sits in

    0 → Ш(E/Q)[p^∞]^∨ → Sel_{p^∞}(E/Q)^∨ → Z_p^2 → 0,

the two `Z_p`'s coming from the rank-`2` Mordell–Weil group of the seed curve.  A control
theorem identifies `Sel_{p^∞}(E/Q)^∨` with the `Γ`-coinvariants `X/TX` of an Iwasawa module
`X`.  That source is **not** a finite bounded object: the Mordell–Weil directions survive in
it, so information about the characteristic ideal of `X` alone does not convert into a bound
for `#Ш[p^∞]`.

## The counterexample, formalized

Take `Λ = Z_p[[T]]` and `X = (Λ/(T))^2`: a torsion `Λ`-module with elementary divisors
`T, T`, hence characteristic ideal `(T^2)`, generated by a distinguished polynomial with unit
leading coefficient.  Nevertheless

    X / TX = X ≅ Z_p^2

is infinite.

Formally, `X` is realized here as `ℤ_[p] × ℤ_[p]` with `Λ` acting through the
constant-coefficient homomorphism (`IwCoinv.moduleLam`).  That action factors through
`Λ/(T)`: the constant-coefficient map is surjective and its kernel is exactly the multiples
of `T` (`IwCoinv.constantCoeff_eq_zero_iff`, `IwCoinv.constantCoeff_surjective`), which is
what makes the elementary-divisor description correct.  `IwCoinv.X_smul_eq_zero` and
`IwCoinv.TX_eq_bot` say `T·X = 0`, and `IwCoinv.instInfiniteQuotient` says the coinvariants
`X/TX` are infinite.

`IwCoinv.infinite_of_surjective_onto_pair` states the same moral without Iwasawa theory: any
group surjecting onto `Z_p^2` is infinite, so the control-theorem source in the displayed
dual Kummer sequence is infinite whatever the size of `Ш`.

Nothing here refutes the use of a main conjecture; it refutes only the inference "unit
leading coefficient ⟹ bounded coinvariants".  The route through a precise leading-term
theorem, primary finiteness, height nondegeneracy and regulator integrality is untouched.
-/

namespace IwCoinv

variable (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime]

/-- The Iwasawa algebra `Λ = Z_p[[T]]`. -/
abbrev Lam := PowerSeries ℤ_[p]

/-- `Z_p` as a `Λ`-module through the constant-coefficient map: this is `Λ/(T)`. -/
noncomputable instance moduleLam : Module (Lam p) ℤ_[p] :=
  Module.compHom ℤ_[p] (PowerSeries.constantCoeff (R := ℤ_[p]))

lemma smul_def (f : Lam p) (a : ℤ_[p]) : f • a = PowerSeries.constantCoeff f * a := rfl

/-- The action factors through `Λ/(T)`: the kernel of the constant-coefficient map is the
ideal of multiples of `T`. -/
lemma constantCoeff_eq_zero_iff (f : Lam p) :
    PowerSeries.constantCoeff f = 0 ↔ (PowerSeries.X : Lam p) ∣ f :=
  PowerSeries.X_dvd_iff.symm

lemma constantCoeff_surjective :
    Function.Surjective (PowerSeries.constantCoeff (R := ℤ_[p])) :=
  fun a => ⟨PowerSeries.C a, by simp⟩

/-- `T` annihilates `Λ/(T)`. -/
lemma X_smul_eq_zero (a : ℤ_[p]) : (PowerSeries.X : Lam p) • a = 0 := by
  rw [smul_def]; simp

instance : Infinite ℤ_[p] := Infinite.of_injective (Nat.cast : ℕ → ℤ_[p]) Nat.cast_injective

/-- The submodule `T · X` of `X = (Λ/(T))^2`. -/
noncomputable def TX : Submodule (Lam p) (ℤ_[p] × ℤ_[p]) :=
  LinearMap.range (LinearMap.lsmul (Lam p) (ℤ_[p] × ℤ_[p]) PowerSeries.X)

lemma TX_eq_bot : TX p = ⊥ := by
  rw [eq_bot_iff]
  rintro x ⟨y, rfl⟩
  simp only [LinearMap.lsmul_apply, Submodule.mem_bot]
  ext <;> simp [Prod.smul_def, X_smul_eq_zero]

/-- The coinvariants `X/TX` are all of `X`. -/
noncomputable def coinvEquiv : ((ℤ_[p] × ℤ_[p]) ⧸ TX p) ≃ₗ[Lam p] (ℤ_[p] × ℤ_[p]) :=
  Submodule.quotEquivOfEqBot _ (TX_eq_bot p)

/-- **The counterexample.**  `X = (Λ/(T))^2` is `Λ`-torsion with characteristic ideal `(T^2)`
— unit leading coefficient — while its `Γ`-coinvariants `X/TX ≅ Z_p^2` are infinite.  A
leading coefficient therefore does not bound the cardinality of the coinvariant group. -/
instance instInfiniteQuotient : Infinite ((ℤ_[p] × ℤ_[p]) ⧸ TX p) :=
  Infinite.of_injective (coinvEquiv p).symm (coinvEquiv p).symm.injective

/-- The same point without Iwasawa theory: a group surjecting onto `Z_p^2` is infinite.  In
`0 → Ш[p^∞]^∨ → Sel_{p^∞}^∨ → Z_p^2 → 0` the middle term — the object a control theorem
produces — is therefore infinite, whatever the size of `Ш`. -/
theorem infinite_of_surjective_onto_pair {G : Type*} [AddCommGroup G]
    (f : G →+ ℤ_[p] × ℤ_[p]) (hf : Function.Surjective f) : Infinite G :=
  Infinite.of_surjective f hf

end IwCoinv
